F-1 (Foxy portability): tf2_sensor_msgs header spelling.

The G1's onboard computer runs ROS 2 Foxy (Ubuntu 20.04) while this workspace
is developed on Humble. Foxy ships tf2_sensor_msgs as `.h`; the `.hpp` spelling
arrived in Galactic. Same header, same doTransform specialisation — selected
with __has_include so the file builds on both.

No behaviour change.
diff --git a/src/laserscan_to_pointcloud_node.cpp b/src/laserscan_to_pointcloud_node.cpp
index 2d2726f..bf45026 100644
--- a/src/laserscan_to_pointcloud_node.cpp
+++ b/src/laserscan_to_pointcloud_node.cpp
@@ -49,7 +49,13 @@
 #include <utility>
 
 #include "sensor_msgs/point_cloud2_iterator.hpp"
+// Foxy ships tf2_sensor_msgs as .h; the .hpp spelling arrived in
+// Galactic. Same header, same doTransform specialisations.
+#if __has_include("tf2_sensor_msgs/tf2_sensor_msgs.hpp")
 #include "tf2_sensor_msgs/tf2_sensor_msgs.hpp"
+#else
+#include "tf2_sensor_msgs/tf2_sensor_msgs.h"
+#endif
 #include "tf2_ros/create_timer_ros.h"
 
 namespace pointcloud_to_laserscan
